  "note": "Election of three town commissioners in place of those retiring by rotation, in the Town Hall on Tuesday 15 January 1901. The outgoing members were B. Woods, Arthur Woods and George M'Bride; James Arthurs and Robert O'Neill were new candidates. Peter M'Knight, town clerk, presiding officer; P. Conry, poll clerk. Poll 8 a.m. to 8 p.m.; \"The first three were declared duly elected.\" No individual party labels are printed (the headline speaks of the \"Dillonites\")."
